 At this time, substitutes were not allowed in the early rounds of the relays, and a runner could only be replaced in the final due to an injury. The Soviets controversially held out 400 gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/77556"} "Viktor Markin"] " in the opening round, instead running " [:a {:href "/athletes/77400"} "Viktor Burakov"] ". But Buryakov developed a mysterious injury before the final, allowing Markin to run. The final was quite close throughout with no more than 1-2 metres separating the USSR and the GDR. The GDR actually had a narrow lead at the bell, and their anchor was run by " [:a {:href "/athletes/69755"} "Volker Beck"] ", gold medalist in the 400 hurdles. But Markin ran him down on the final lap, and won by slightly over a metre. The winning time was the slowest since the 1960 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Soviet Union"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "3:01.8 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:01.1 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/77698"} "Remigijus Valiulis"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77539"} "Mikhail Linge"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77405"} "Nikolay Chernetsky"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77556"} "Viktor Markin"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/77400"} "Viktor Burakov"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/923697"} "Sergey Lovachov"] [:small {} " (DNS)"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "East Germany"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middl